From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:35:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 103/138] irqchip: Add a driver for the Apple PMIC event
 interrupts

The D2186 PMU keeps its events at 0x50..0x5c (cleared by reading them,
which is all iOS does to "clear events"), the current levels at
0x60..0x6d and one mask bit per event at 0x70..0x7c (1 = masked, iOS
masks all at start). Event 3 is VBUS detect, 24..44 are the PMU GPIO
inputs and 88 is the RTC alarm. Layout from the iOS 12 AppleD2186PMU
driver; the PMU line goes to AP GPIO 106, active low.

Expose the events as a nested threaded irq domain. Everything is masked
at probe and only events with a user get unmasked. Across system sleep
only wake enabled events stay unmasked, like iOS before sleep; events of
other users that arrive meanwhile are delivered on resume.

The driver must not take the system down with it: a storm (more than
100 runs a second, or 20 runs in a row without an event) or 10 I2C errors
in a row switch the parent interrupt off with one message. The domain is
registered even when the parent interrupt is missing or disabled with
irq_apple_pmic.enable=0, so the users of the events still probe. A
debugfs file shows the masks, status registers and event counts.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
